1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,400
the investigation into Malia Bass's death depended on more than the conflicting accounts

2
00:00:05,400 --> 00:00:11,433
given by the adults responsible for her care detectives had to test those accounts against witness statements

3
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:16,500
photographs recorded police interactions and other available evidence

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:20,300
each line of inquiry offered a way to assess whether the explanation

5
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:25,666
provided on August 22 matched what investigators could independently establish

6
00:00:25,666 --> 00:00:29,766
one important source was the 911 call reporting Malia missing

7
00:00:29,766 --> 00:00:33,600
according to the search warrant account described by the Houston Chronicle

8
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:37,866
Sahara Irvin said Traevion Thompson had been asleep investigator

9
00:00:37,866 --> 00:00:43,966
compared that statement with another reported version in which Thompson allegedly called Irvin inside

10
00:00:43,966 --> 00:00:48,400
to prepare food the accounts raised a specific question

11
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:54,066
what had Thompson actually been doing during the period when Malia was supposedly outside

12
00:00:54,066 --> 00:00:57,100
the discrepancy required further examination

13
00:00:57,100 --> 00:01:01,333
although a contradiction alone could not establish that a crime had occurred

14
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:06,733
Thompson's descriptions of his own activities also reportedly differed in one account

15
00:01:06,733 --> 00:01:12,100
he said he had been playing video games in another he described sweeping the floor

16
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:18,066
detectives had to consider these differences alongside the timing of the reported disappearance

17
00:01:18,066 --> 00:01:24,466
and the other evidence they were collecting the significance lay not simply in the existence of different versions

18
00:01:24,466 --> 00:01:28,800
but in whether either account could be supported by independent information

19
00:01:28,800 --> 00:01:35,400
investigators also examined the apartment itself according to the search warrant reporting they reviewed photographs

20
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:40,533
and found no evidence that the kitchen had been used in the way described in the breakfast account

21
00:01:40,533 --> 00:01:46,166
that observation gave detectives a reason to question the proposed sequence of events

22
00:01:46,166 --> 00:01:51,733
it was not by itself conclusive proof that breakfast had not been prepared

23
00:01:51,733 --> 00:01:55,900
but it provided another detail to compare with the adult statements

24
00:01:55,900 --> 00:02:00,600
another account came from an upstairs neighbor according to the Sir warrant documents

25
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:05,333
the neighbor told police he had been outside drinking coffee and smoking around the time

26
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:11,200
Malia was reportedly playing near the playground but had not seen either Malia or Irvin there

27
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:15,933
investigators considered this relevant because the neighbor's reported observations

28
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:20,766
did not support the location and timing described by the adults still

29
00:02:20,766 --> 00:02:27,166
his statement represented one witness's account not a complete record of everything that occurred at the complex

30
00:02:27,166 --> 00:02:31,866
police also deployed a trained tracking dog the search warrant report stated that

31
00:02:31,866 --> 00:02:35,066
Irvin and Thompson objected to the dog's involvement

32
00:02:35,066 --> 00:02:39,733
as the dog moved toward a nearby field the adults reportedly stopped the handler

33
00:02:39,733 --> 00:02:44,766
and attempted to direct him back toward the apartment complex they then reiterated that

34
00:02:44,766 --> 00:02:49,466
I did not want the dog used investigators documented these interactions

35
00:02:49,466 --> 00:02:55,100
as part of their assessment of the search the objections did not independently establish guilt

36
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:59,666
but they became another issue examined alongside the other discrepancies

37
00:02:59,666 --> 00:03:03,400
body camera footage provided a further record of the response

38
00:03:03,400 --> 00:03:10,000
investigators reviewed the officer's interactions with the adults and concluded in their account that neither

39
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:13,300
appeared to make an effort to search for the missing child

40
00:03:13,300 --> 00:03:18,333
that was the investigator's interpretation of the recorded behavior rather than a separate

41
00:03:18,333 --> 00:03:24,266
forensic finding the footage nevertheless gave investigators material they could review

42
00:03:24,266 --> 00:03:29,800
beyond later recollections and interviews the inquiry also extended to digital records

43
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:35,933
a search warrant sought access to Irvin's Facebook account allowing investigators to look for information

44
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:42,166
relevant to the case the published reporting identifies the warrants purpose but does not establish

45
00:03:42,166 --> 00:03:47,700
that any particular social media post proved what happened to Malia the investigate

46
00:03:47,700 --> 00:03:52,000
involved Houston Police Department personnel including investigators A

47
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:56,566
Henderson and E Russo who were named in the department's official release

48
00:03:56,566 --> 00:04:01,766
concerning the case their work alongside the broader massacre investigation

49
00:04:01,766 --> 00:04:07,933
brought together the initial report witness accounts recorded interactions and other evidence

50
00:04:07,933 --> 00:04:13,733
no single inconsistency resolved the case the significance emerged from the cumulative record

51
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:18,966
and from how closely the original explanation held up when investigators tested it against

52
00:04:18,966 --> 00:04:24,400
independent observations surveillance footage became an important part of the investigation

53
00:04:24,400 --> 00:04:28,700
because it offered a record investigators could compare with the accounts given by Malia

54
00:04:28,700 --> 00:04:34,733
Bass's caregivers according to search warrant reporting footage showed Malia with Sahara Irvin

55
00:04:34,733 --> 00:04:38,700
and Travyon Thompson during a convenience store trip around midnight

56
00:04:38,700 --> 00:04:44,533
on August 20th, 2020 the recording helped investigators establish an earlier point

57
00:04:44,533 --> 00:04:49,533
in the timeline although it did not reveal everything that happened afterward

58
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:56,333
investigators then examined footage from the night of August 21 according to the reported search warrant account

59
00:04:56,333 --> 00:05:01,866
Thompson was seen carrying a large trash can and moving toward a storm drain area

60
00:05:01,866 --> 00:05:05,500
Irvin was reportedly waiting outside while he left the apartment

61
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:10,066
Thompson later returned and the couple subsequently went to a convenience store

62
00:05:10,066 --> 00:05:16,300
the footage did not by itself establish what was inside the trash can or show the full circumstances

63
00:05:16,300 --> 00:05:22,733
surrounding Malaya's death investigators had to interpret the recorded movements alongside other evidence

64
00:05:22,733 --> 00:05:27,166
and statements obtained during the inquiry the distinction mattered

65
00:05:27,166 --> 00:05:33,600
surveillance could document visible actions but it could not automatically explain the purpose behind them

66
00:05:33,600 --> 00:05:39,800
investigators also reviewed available footage for evidence supporting the original missing child account

67
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:46,600
according to reporting on the search warrant they found no recording showing Malia wandering away from the complex

68
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:52,800
or an apparent abductor leaving with her that absence did not prove precisely what happened but

69
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:57,900
it meant the investigators had not found surveillance support for those possible scenarios

70
00:05:57,900 --> 00:06:02,966
the search warrant account also stated that investigators could not locate a pillowcase

71
00:06:02,966 --> 00:06:08,266
and wooden blocks that Thompson had described in a public account their absence became another

72
00:06:08,266 --> 00:06:12,900
unresolved point in the inquiry rather than independent proof of a particular

73
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:15,400
sequence of events after his arrest

74
00:06:15,400 --> 00:06:19,766
Thompson reportedly admitted disposing of Malia's body in a storm drain

75
00:06:19,766 --> 00:06:25,600
connected to Brays Bayou that reported admission was distinct from the surveillance footage

76
00:06:25,600 --> 00:06:31,933
the recording documented movements while the statement attributed to Thompson addressed what he said had happened

77
00:06:31,933 --> 00:06:35,633
together the footage the missing items and

78
00:06:35,633 --> 00:06:41,133
Thompson's reported admission helped investigators examine how the body reached the Bayou

79
00:06:41,133 --> 00:06:44,800
none should be mistaken for a recording of the assault itself

80
00:06:44,800 --> 00:06:50,100
the case depended on evaluating each piece of evidence within the broader investigation

81
00:06:50,100 --> 00:06:55,000
for Malia Bass's family the investigation was not simply a criminal case

82
00:06:55,000 --> 00:07:00,533
it was the search for answers about a child whose life had ended at just 2 years old

83
00:07:00,533 --> 00:07:05,366
her grandmother Rosalie Jimerson spoke publicly about her granddaughter

84
00:07:05,366 --> 00:07:10,533
and the family's demand for justice her comments gave a personal dimension to a case

85
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:15,733
increasingly discussed through evidence court records and legal arguments

86
00:07:15,733 --> 00:07:22,133
Maliyah's father Octavius Bass also formed part of the family's experience of the loss

87
00:07:22,133 --> 00:07:28,566
as the case moved through the justice system relatives faced the difficult reality of seeking accountability

88
00:07:28,566 --> 00:07:34,166
while grieving a child they could not bring back the case drew public attention across Houston

89
00:07:34,166 --> 00:07:38,566
with community concern focused on how a vulnerable toddler had died

90
00:07:38,566 --> 00:07:42,200
and whether those responsible would face consequences

91
00:07:42,200 --> 00:07:47,666
public statements and courtroom appearances kept Malia's family at the center of the story

92
00:07:47,666 --> 00:07:54,533
reminding observers that behind the investigation was a little girl remembered and loved by those closest to her

93
00:07:54,533 --> 00:08:01,266
in October 2020 the investigation into Malia Bass's death moved into criminal proceedings

94
00:08:01,266 --> 00:08:06,766
Sahara Irvin and Travyon Thompson were questioned as detectives continued examining the accounts

95
00:08:06,766 --> 00:08:10,800
given after Malia was reported missing the medical findings

96
00:08:10,800 --> 00:08:16,933
witness information and surveillance evidence on October 7th the Houston Police Department

97
00:08:16,933 --> 00:08:22,666
announced that both adults had been charged with injury to a child with serious bodily injury

98
00:08:22,666 --> 00:08:29,100
and tampering with evidence involving a human corpse the charges reflected two distinct allegations

99
00:08:29,100 --> 00:08:34,800
that a child had suffered serious injury through criminal conduct and that evidence connected with a death

100
00:08:34,800 --> 00:08:40,066
had been concealed or altered at this stage the charges were accusations

101
00:08:40,066 --> 00:08:44,166
not findings of guilt contemporaneous reporting described different

102
00:08:44,166 --> 00:08:50,866
early bond decisions Thompson was denied bond with his probation status reported as a factor

103
00:08:50,866 --> 00:08:56,733
Irvin's bond across the charges was set at a combined $175,000

104
00:08:56,733 --> 00:09:03,200
those decisions concerned whether and under what conditions the accused could be released while the case proceeded

105
00:09:03,200 --> 00:09:10,133
they were not determinations of guilt the prosecution had to establish a legal basis for moving forward

106
00:09:10,133 --> 00:09:16,800
search warrant materials were relevant because they recorded the investigative grounds for examining inconsistencies

107
00:09:16,800 --> 00:09:20,600
in the caregivers accounts and pursuing additional evidence

108
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:26,266
a warrant affidavit can explain why investigators believe evidence may be found

109
00:09:26,266 --> 00:09:31,533
or why a suspect may be connected to an offence probable cause however

110
00:09:31,533 --> 00:09:38,533
is a lower threshold than proof beyond a reasonable doubt it supports investigative and procedural steps

111
00:09:38,533 --> 00:09:44,200
it does not by itself establish guilt at trial the case involved prosecutors

112
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:48,766
from the Harris County District Attorney's Office including Lacey Johnson

113
00:09:48,766 --> 00:09:54,566
who LED its child fatality division and Assistant District Attorney Edward Applebaum

114
00:09:54,566 --> 00:10:00,766
Kim OG was the county district attorney when the case reached its 2024 resolution

115
00:10:00,766 --> 00:10:05,466
Irvin was represented during earlier proceedings by attorney Angela Welton

116
00:10:05,466 --> 00:10:11,800
while reporting identified Tyrone Moncrief as Thompson's attorney the charges filed in 2020

117
00:10:11,800 --> 00:10:16,133
must be distinguished from the offenses ultimately resolved through guilty pleas

118
00:10:16,133 --> 00:10:22,200
no jury verdict followed a contested trial instead the legal process continued

119
00:10:22,200 --> 00:10:26,533
through plea agreements and sentencing with each defendant's admissions

120
00:10:26,533 --> 00:10:30,256
defining the offenses to which that person formally pleaded guilty
